From 3ff9e5a4198313110b5b500073be5a2d9b775e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kush Kumar <kush@Mac.vodafone.ultrahub>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 09:45:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ClusterSecretStore namespace bypass (CVSS 8.0)

Add provider-level namespace validation as defense-in-depth for
ClusterSecretStore operations. The PrivX provider's GetSecret() and
GetAllSecrets() methods now enforce namespace isolation when a
ClusterSecretStore has spec.conditions restricting access.

Changes:
- Add ErrNamespaceNotAllowed sentinel error
- Implement namespaceMatchesCondition() helper (checks Namespaces list
  and NamespaceRegexes patterns)
- Implement validateNamespaceAccess() method on SecretsClient
- Add namespace validation guard at the top of GetSecret()
- Add namespace validation guard at the top of GetAllSecrets()
- Add unit tests for namespace bypass rejection (4 tests)
- Add property-based preservation tests for authorized access (9 tests)
- Promote golang-jwt/jwt/v5 from indirect to direct dependency

The fix matches the pattern used by other built-in ESO providers and
complements the controller-level shouldProcessSecret() check.

Resolves: ClusterSecretStore namespace bypass vulnerability
Requirements: 2.3, 2.4, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4
